Hello,

I believe I have found an error in the R-INLA faq. In answer 22 (https://www.r-inla.org/faq#h.z4ecbkezo5tu) there is a link to a techincal report (in this tech-report <https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fsites.google.com%2Fa%2Fr-inla.org%2Fwww%2Ffaq%2Fwaic_understand3.pdf%3Fattredirects%3D0&sa=D&sntz=1&usg=AOvVaw2JH_cV898Iez_DoAx-DQkA>) that goes to a resource that does not exist.

After some digging I found a document with the same name as given in the link URL in the Github repository <https://github.com/hrue/r-inla/blob/devel/internal-doc/waic/waic_understand3.pdf>.  This document seems to be the same as Gelman et al. 2014(DOI: 10.1007/s11222-013-9416-2 <https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11222-013-9416-2>).

Could this be changed in the faq to either cite the paper or in some other way give reference to the article to make it findable?

Thanks in advance,
Kristian

