Hi all,

I’m working through the
multinomial example provided in the INBO/INLA vignette:

https://rdrr.io/github/inbo/INLA/f/vignettes/multinomial.Rmd

I would like to extract
the predicted probabilities of choosing alternative at the mesh
locations for the continuous spatial random effect example.

So far, I’ve tried
creating a separate prediction stack over the mesh and combining it
with the original estimation stack. The model runs fine. However, I’m
struggling to extract spatial predictions on the mesh using
inla.mesh.projector.

Specifically, I'm not
sure how to project the posterior means back onto the mesh for
visualization for every single choosing alternative.

Any guidance or working
example on how to do this properly in the multinomial setting would
be greatly appreciated.

Thanks in advance!

Miguel

